<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 6.4 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 6.4 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 6.4 percent in the week to March 19 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 6.2 percent.(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			   Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation  20.85	  20.74	     19.56</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	 1.94	   2.08		1.78</p>
</text>
